  "purpose": "Where Mathlib's declarations lie on the disk: the area of a module is the area of the longest prefix below that names it, whole components only (Mathlib.Topology names Mathlib.Topology.Basic but not Mathlib.Topologyx). An area is an arXiv category of the map (scripts/arxiv_groups.py), or one of its finer areas (data/arxiv-subareas.json) as math.NT/analytic; null leaves the modules out of the disk and out of every count (tactics and tooling). A first pass, by Mathlib's folders and arXiv's descriptions of its categories (field theory goes with number fields, as arXiv's math.NT lists Galois theory; measure theory with functional analysis, as math.FA lists it; homological algebra with category theory, as math.CT lists it). Edit a line to move a folder.",
